Feature: slice-5 / flutter-web-therapist-console
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-5
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.3 (Flutter Web therapist console)

What was built
==============
Audited and adapted the existing therapist-console flows to run on
web. The bulk of the code is already platform-agnostic; we shipped
one targeted kIsWeb branch and confirmed the rest builds + analyzes
cleanly.

Code change (one file):
- lib/screens/new_session_screen.dart — kIsWeb branch in the CTA
  cluster: on web, the recording button disappears entirely and
  "WGRAJ PLIK AUDIO" is the only (primary, Ember-glow) CTA. On
  iOS the existing "ROZPOCZNIJ NAGRYWANIE" primary + "Wgraj plik
  audio" secondary ordering is preserved. Matches docs/18 §8.3
  "New session — file upload still available; recording branch
  hidden on web."

Already platform-agnostic, no changes needed
============================================
Inspected every therapist-console screen for dart:io / Platform.* /
File() / Directory() usages. Only three screens have any:
  - recording_screen.dart        — already kIsWeb-guarded (feature 1)
  - new_session_screen.dart      — kIsWeb-branched (this feature)
  - menu_screen.dart             — avatar-upload File(picked.path)
                                   at line 97; feature 4
                                   (flutter-web-profile-edit)
                                   territory. Doesn't crash on web
                                   build; only fails at runtime if a
                                   user clicks the avatar.

Screens with NO platform code (all run as-is on web):
  - home_screen.dart                (Kartoteki list)
  - client_details_screen.dart      (patient details + session list)
  - session_details_screen.dart     (single session)
  - session_status_screen.dart      (Firestore-listener stepper)
  - transcript_screen.dart          (player + PDF export via pdfx)
  - report_screen.dart              (sections + risk badge)
  - subscription_plan_screen.dart   (billing read-only)
  - pending_uploads_screen.dart     (upload queue)
  - login_screen.dart               (Firebase Auth)
  - delete_account_screen.dart      (account removal flow)
  - legal_markdown_screen.dart      (Terms/Privacy/DPA viewer)
  - legal_pdf_screen.dart           (legacy PDF viewer)
  - therapist_setup_screen.dart     (onboarding)

Core data layer (already web-ready):
- lib/services/grpc_client.dart uses `GrpcOrGrpcWebClientChannel`
  from package:grpc — auto-selects HTTP/2 on iOS/Android and
  gRPC-Web over HTTPS on the browser. No code change needed.
- lib/firebase_options.dart includes the kIsWeb platform branch
  from the original `flutter create --platforms web` scaffold.
- Firestore listeners (session-status stepper) work via the
  firebase_js_sdk facade that cloud_firestore web ships with.
- audioplayers + pdfx packages have web platform support (with
  the Wasm dry-run warnings docs/18 §8.3 flags as acceptable
  under CanvasKit/HTML renderer).

How verified
============
1. `flutter analyze lib` → No issues found (4.1s). Captured at
   evidence/.../analyze.log.
2. `flutter build web --no-tree-shake-icons --no-wasm-dry-run` →
   "✓ Built build/web" in 68s. Bundle still 45 MB.
3. Served the bundle (python3 -m http.server 8765) and hit it
   with puppeteer at desktop viewport — login screen renders
   correctly with Polish strings and Euphire tokens
   (evidence/.../login-pl-full.png).
4. Source audit (grep dart:io, Platform., File(, Directory() in
   lib/screens/) showed only the three flagged screens; the rest
   are pure platform-agnostic Flutter widgets + Riverpod +
   gRPC-OrWeb + Firebase Web SDK calls.

What's NOT live-verified in this session (deferred)
====================================================
The Kartoteki / session-details / transcript / report screens
can't be screenshotted without an authenticated SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN
user or seeded test data — same constraint that hit every
backend-dependent feature in Slices 3 + 4. Two paths to live
evidence:
  - Slice 5 feature 8 (registration-e2e style) — Playwright suite
    against the Flutter Web bundle with Firebase emulator + gRPC
    intercepts.
  - End-to-end against staging once Cloud Build deploys this
    branch via the existing `superwizor-app` Firebase Hosting
    site config (firebase.json from Slice 2 feature 8).
Both are infra-only follow-ups; the code that walks those flows
is the SAME code paths the iOS app already exercises in
production.

Compliance with docs/18 §8.3
============================
- ✓ Recording screen replaced with iPhone-app CTA (feature 1).
- ✓ New-session recording branch hidden on web, file upload
  becomes primary CTA (this feature).
- ✓ File picker via file_picker package — already had web
  support; existing Wgraj-plik path works unchanged on web.
- ✓ Audio playback uses audioplayers (web supported).
- ✓ PDF export uses pdfx (web supported).
- ☐ Avatar upload `<input type="file">` swap — feature 4.
- ☐ FCM push (browser PWA-style) — explicitly out of MVP per
  §8.3.
- ☐ Shared-machine warning — Slice 6 polish.

